## Awards built around the event

Custom sports medals combine event identity, achievement and presentation in one coordinated award. Build the design around the sport, then allow space for the event name, year, distance, division or placement. The medal and ribbon should carry the same visual identity from podium photographs to the finished keepsake.

## Shape, relief and color

Choose zinc alloy, iron or brass according to the size, shape and relief. Two-level artwork suits logos, text and enamel color blocks; sculpted 3D elements add depth to athletes, mascots and equipment. Custom outlines and cutouts can make the sport or event theme part of the silhouette.

Bright, antique, matte, black and double-plated finishes can be paired with enamel or metal-only detail. Four hanging-loop styles and a choice of heat-transfer, jacquard or screen-printed ribbon allow the neckwear to match the medal. Chains and twisted cords provide alternative presentation options.

## From artwork to award

The approved proof defines both faces, relief, color, hanging point and ribbon artwork before tooling. After metal forming and finishing, the neckwear is assembled and checked with the medal for clear detail, consistent color and secure attachment. Coordinate related designs across age groups, race distances or tournament placements.

## Plan your order

The minimum order is 50 pieces. Typical production takes 12-18 business days, excluding shipping. Send the event logo, sport, date, size, quantities by division, ribbon preference and destination. Races, team tournaments, school sports days and corporate fitness events can each use a tailored medal and ribbon combination.
